 "description": "<p>The Government is responsible for the daily operations of the Government of Greenland. The Cabinet works all the year round.&nbsp;The Parliament appoints the Premier, who then appoints her Cabinet of ministers. The&nbsp;Government is divided into ministries, each headed by a minister. In the ministries departments handle the prac&shy;tical administrative work. The mini&shy;sters are politically responsible for the work of these departments.&nbsp;The Government&rsquo;s administration must be performed within the frame&shy;works adopted by the Greenland Parliament in the form of acts and appropriations. The Greenland Parliament supervises the Cabinet&rsquo;s work through, for example, audits of the Accounts of the Greenland Treasury. The Cabinet&rsquo;s administration is also super&shy;vised by an ombudsman who keeps an eye on the Cabinet&rsquo;s admi&shy;nistration to ensure that it is in accordance with the legislation and good administration practice. Source:&nbsp;http://naalakkersuisut.gl/en/Naalakkersuisut</p>",
